#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:281
msgid ""
"Sequential `.await` calls *appear* ordered from the host's perspective (each "
"waits before the next starts), but the GPU work for each `.await` runs on "
"whichever stream the policy assigns. For truly independent operations you "
"want to overlap, use `zip!` or `tokio::join!`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:286
msgid "CUDA Graphs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:288
msgid ""
"A CUDA graph captures a composed `DeviceOp` into a pre-compiled executable. "
"Launching the executable submits the entire graph in a single driver call — "
"no per-op dispatch overhead — and the same graph can be replayed many times. "
"This matters for hot paths like per-token inference loops, where individual "
"kernels run in microseconds and launch overhead dominates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:290
msgid "Two capture APIs, depending on how you want to express the pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:292
msgid ""
"// Combinator form — capture what a DeviceOp chain produces.\n"
"let graph = pipeline(input).graph_on(stream.clone())?;\n"
"\n"
"// Scope form — imperative capture when you need &mut between steps.\n"
"let graph = CudaGraph::scope(&stream, |s| {\n"
"    s.record(kernel_a((&mut out_a).partition([32]), x.clone()))?;\n"
"    s.record(kernel_b((&mut out_b).partition([32]), x))?;\n"
"    Ok(())\n"
"})?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:304
msgid ""
"Once captured, replay with `graph.launch()`, which returns a `DeviceOp` you "
"can sync, await, or compose further. For parameterized replay — the common "
"\"change one input per step\" case — `graph.update(new_op)` rewrites the "
"graph's inputs in place without re-instantiating:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:306
msgid ""
"for token in tokens {\n"
"    graph.update(api::memcpy(&mut model.input, &token))?;\n"
"    graph.launch().sync_on(&stream)?;  // no per-op dispatch\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:313
msgid ""
"Only operations that implement the `GraphNode` trait can be recorded: kernel "
"launches and `memcpy`. Allocation operations (`api::zeros`, `api::ones`, "
"etc.) are not graph-safe — allocate outside the capture closure and pass the "
"tensors in. Inside a `scope` body, calling `.sync_on(...)`, `.sync()`, or "
"`.await` on any `DeviceOp` returns a `DeviceError`: the execution lock "
"rejects nested execution during capture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:315
msgid ""
"See [Tutorial 10: CUDA Graphs](../tutorials/10-cuda-graphs.md) for a "
"walkthrough and [Host API: CUDA Graph Integration](../reference/host-"
"api.md#cuda-graph-integration) for the full API reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:320
msgid "Passing tensors and reading results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:322
msgid ""
"Kernel `&Tensor` params accept three input forms, and `&mut Tensor` params "
"accept two partition forms. You get back the same type you put in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:324
msgid "Read-only inputs (`&Tensor`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:326
msgid ""
"// Owned — single use, no Arc overhead.\n"
"let x: Tensor<f32> = ones(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let (_, x) = kernel(out, x).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"\n"
"// Shared — use the same tensor in multiple kernels.\n"
"let x: Arc<Tensor<f32>> = ones(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?.into();\n"
"let z1 = kernel1(out1, x.clone()).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let z2 = kernel2(out2, x.clone()).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"\n"
"// Borrowed — no allocation, borrow checker enforces lifetime.\n"
"let x: Tensor<f32> = ones(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let _ = kernel(out, &x).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:341
msgid "Mutable outputs (`&mut Tensor`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:343
msgid ""
"// Owned partition — must unpartition() to get the tensor back.\n"
"let z = zeros(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?.partition([4, 4]);\n"
"let (z, ..) = kernel(z, &x).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let tensor = z.unpartition();\n"
"\n"
"// Borrowed partition — writes in place, no unpartition() needed.\n"
"let mut z = zeros(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let _ = kernel((&mut z).partition([4, 4]), &x).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:354
msgid ""
"Borrowed inputs and borrowed partitions aren't `'static`, so `tokio::spawn` "
"rejects them at compile time — use `Arc` and owned partitions for spawned "
"tasks. See the [Host API: Ownership Model](../reference/host-"
"api.md#ownership-model) for the full ownership model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:356
msgid ""
"Host readback is itself a `DeviceOp`. Constructing it is lazy; sync or await "
"the readback op before using the host data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:358
msgid ""
"// Bad: constructs a host copy operation, but never executes it.\n"
"let z = kernel(x, y).first().sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let data_op = z.to_host_vec();\n"
"\n"
"// Good: execute the copy before reading the Vec.\n"
"let z = kernel(x, y).first().sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"let data = z.to_host_vec().sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:370
msgid "Runtime Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:372
msgid ""
"**Execution lock.** cuTile enforces \"only one `DeviceOp` executes per "
"thread at a time.\" Nesting `.sync_on(...)`, `.sync()`, or `.await` inside a "
"`.then(...)` closure or a `CudaGraph::scope` body returns a `DeviceError`. "
"The lock exists to prevent cross-stream data races: a nested "
"`sync_on(&other_stream)` inside a `.then()` handler would submit work to a "
"second stream without ordering it against the first. For the rare legitimate "
"case, use `unsafe fn then_unchecked`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:374
msgid ""
"**Default device.** The device each `DeviceOp` lands on is thread-local. "
"`set_default_device(id)` changes it for the current thread — the common "
"pattern for one-thread-per-GPU worker pools. For per-op routing without "
"touching the thread default, get a policy with `global_policy(id)` or "
"`with_device_policy(id, |policy| ...)` and call `op.schedule(&policy)?`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:376
msgid ""
"Handles from other frameworks (cudarc, Candle, hand-rolled FFI) can be "
"wrapped into a cuTile `Device` or `Stream` without transferring ownership "
"via `Device::borrow_raw` / `Stream::borrow_raw` — see [Interoperability]"
"(interoperability.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/device-operations.md:380
msgid ""
"Continue to [Performance](performance.md) for optimization techniques. For "
"the full `DeviceOp` API, see the [Host API](../reference/host-api.md)."
msgstr ""
